  "rawCandidate" : "{\"plan\":{\"update\":\"replace\",\"text\":\"Develop diamonds immediately: nine tricks can come from two spades, two hearts, two clubs and three diamonds, including the spade already won. Lead D3 toward dummy's king, normally following with the queen when appropriate, and concede another diamond if needed to establish the length. A 3–3 diamond break supplies three tricks for two concessions; other breaks require reassessment from the actual cards. Preserve dummy's club ace as the entry to established diamonds, and retain South's club king and heart winners for communication. If defenders return spades, use the queen as the remaining stopper and continue diamonds promptly. Avoid cashing side winners prematurely. The main risks are unfavorable diamonds and a long defensive spade holding; adjust the diamond continuation to revealed honors and distribution rather than assuming the suit will run.\"},\"selectedCard\":\"D3\",\"publicReason\":\"Diamonds are the essential source of three additional tricks. Start developing them now while the spade queen still provides a stopper and dummy's club ace remains an entry.\"}",
  "rawReview" : "{\n  \"verdict\": \"revise\",\n  \"blockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The proposed diamond sequence can exhaust dummy's entry before its length is established, even on a 3–3 break.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"For example, let West hold DT86 and East DAJ2. On D3–D6–DK–D2, the king wins. Dummy's queen then loses to East's ace, exhausting South's diamonds. After a spade return to SQ, CA is needed to reach dummy and concede a third diamond to DJ. Dummy's remaining D75 are winners, but the stated route has no remaining assured entry to cash them. Preserving South's CK and heart winners does not provide an entry to North.\",\n      \"requestedChange\": \"Replace the king-first sequence with an entry-safe development plan. For example, duck the first diamond in dummy, then lead South's remaining diamond toward the honors after recovering control. Explain how CA is retained until the necessary concessions are complete. D3 itself can remain the selected card.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"advisorySuggestions\": []\n}",
